From: François Guerraz <kubrick@fgv6.net>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: S-R control files

The S-R mode has been driven by nothing so far. This patch adds the five
debugfs files its one controller, /usr/sbin/ppe-sr, uses (WP3-DESIGN
§4.1), next to the offload's own:

  offload_sr         0600  arm <s> [offers] | offers on|off |
                           deadline <s> | disarm | uninhibit <gen>
  offload_sr_scope   0600  class <port> <U|T> <vid> | client any|<a.b.c.d>
                           | commit
  offload_sr_status  0400  the status, from memory alone
  offload_sr_hw      0400  the idle verify and the identities' counters
  offload_sr_guard   0200  "1": the bounded disarm without RTNL

A write returns its length or the error of what it ran, and each verb is
counted. arm and deadline take seconds from 60 to 86400; uninhibit takes
the generation read from the status before the enable began, so that a
stop that overlapped the enable keeps arms refused.

The locks follow the existing order: the parameter lock, RTNL, the
offload lock. arm takes all three; while RTNL is busy the write restarts
rather than wait unkillably, since rtnl_lock_killable() is not exported.
offers and deadline take the parameter lock and the offload lock; disarm,
uninhibit and the reads only the offload lock, killably; the guard the
offload lock only, for 2 s at most. The parameter lock also checks that
the file's offload is still the instance.

A scope is written as lines and put in force by a commit, which sorts the
classes, refuses a class given twice or classes without a client line,
and denies everything when no class is given. Lines may be split across
writes; each write takes the parameter lock and RTNL before it parses, so
that a restart finds the open file's edit unchanged and two writers of
one file are serialized. A line that does not parse fails its write and
every later commit on that open file. A port outside 0-9, a VID outside
1-4094 or in 3900-3919, a malformed address, more than 330 classes or 64
clients, or "client any" with a list are such lines.

The status is printed from a copy taken under the lock, as "key value"
lines in a fixed order, and calls no register accessor. offload_stop()
removes the files before it takes any lock.

Signed-off-by: François Guerraz <kubrick@fgv6.net>
